  "findings": [
    "Four selected raw-column statistics are visible to the transformer and none to the reader; absence from reader pg_stats is visibility evidence, not proof statistics do not exist.",
    "All four common mart plan numeric summaries are identical across roles; this comparison does not support attributing these estimate differences to reader privileges.",
    "Raw and directly normalized item-ID grouping both estimate87208 groups; staging and mart grouping estimate200. The direct NULLIF expression alone does not reproduce the loss.",
    "Staging order and item view reloptions are null: neither currently specifies security_barrier. No security option was changed.",
    "Raw delivered-status estimate96454 becomes49720 with the normalized/coalesced predicate. Typed period and combined filters retain low estimates; parallel scan estimates are per plan node/worker, not measured totals.",
    "No extended statistics objects on the two raw tables. Analysis counters/timestamps are zero/absent despite existing column statistics; these counters do not prove ANALYZE never occurred.",
    "PostgreSQL17 stable-branch source rejects subquery pull-up when a WITH list is present. This supports a controlled CTE-boundary hypothesis; it is not yet measured proof for a rewritten model."
  ],
  "next": "Prepare a new read-only EXPLAIN-only pair grouping the same normalized raw.order_items ID through an ordinary derived SELECT versus an otherwise identical WITH-containing subquery. Keep expressions, collation and role equal. If the estimate changes, review a CTE-free staging projection before source changes, preserving all columns, parsing/missingness/lineage and independent tests. No statistics mutation or package needed for this first comparison.",
